<title>UK: IGC raises forecast for 96 world coarse grains crop.</title>
<headline>IGC raises forecast for 96 world coarse grains crop.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>World coarse grains production should reach 892 million tonnes in 1996, sharply higher than the 799 million turned out in 1995, the International Grains Council (IGC) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The IGC's previous estimate, issued in May, was for 889 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The IGC also raised its forecast for 1996 coarse grains consumption by four million tonnes to 869 million, although its reduced its stocks forecast by one million to 113 million.</p>
<p>World coarse grains consumption totalled 828 million tonnes in 1995, with stocks at 90 million, the IGC said.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
</text>
